US-051 (GPU particles) is **Partial**. Every gate this environment can run passes on the final tree, except the GCC rebuild of the last cleanup edit and the native Linux GPU and benchmark runs. I did not mark it complete, and I did not emit the completion signal.

**Implemented**
- **Particle system** (`engine/render/src/particles.cpp`, `include/engine/render/particles.hpp`, `shaders/particles.hlsl`): emitters with lifetime, velocity cone, gravity, colour and size curves (8 keys), spawn radius, bounds, and seeded spawns. Compute emit and simulate, an atomic live counter, and an indirect draw of textured billboards.
- **Blend and depth:** alpha and additive blend. Billboards test against the scene depth and do not write it.
- **Budgets:** per-emitter capacity, a system particle budget, and an emitter count. Overflow is clamped to capacity and counted as dropped; the ring overwrites the oldest slots.
- **Lifecycle:** pause, reset, and emitter removal. Removal destroys the emitter's five buffers and three descriptor sets.
- **RHI:** a new `PipelineDesc::additive_blend` flag, implemented on DX12 and Vulkan, with contract tests.
- **Docs:** `docs/particles.md`, and a progress-log entry with Codebase Patterns.

**Choices I made (the PRD leaves these open)**
- Textures are read with `Load`, because the RHI has no sampler descriptor.
- Each emitter owns its own GPU buffers, so removal releases them directly.
- The system can't be created on the CPU reference device, since it needs uploads. Budget, pause, reset, and deletion are tested on the GPU.
- Reproducibility is checked within one backend. Two seeded runs must match byte for byte.

**Verification (final tree unless noted)**

| Gate | Result |
|---|---|
| Windows ValidateVendor, win-dev, win-debug, win-unit | pass (21/21 unit) |
| Windows `engine_tests --suite gpu --backend dx12` | pass, 71 cases |
| Windows `engine_tests --suite gpu --backend vulkan` | pass, 72 cases |
| Linux clang debug build and unit ctest | pass (22/22) |
| Linux ASan/UBSan build and sanitize ctest | pass (22/22, 0 build warnings) |
| Linux GCC build and unit ctest | pass on the tree before my last cleanup; not rebuilt with the cleaned file |

